{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# Generalize divergent-head healing: share reconcile_one across sync and the S3 doctor\n\n## Disposition: OBSOLETE — the targeted duplication was removed by Gerrit 1665\n\nThis ticket asked for a shared, behaviour-preserving `reconcile_one(tracker, target_ref)` used by\nboth `sync.reconverge` and `s3_doctor._fold_heads`. Premise validation disproved it. The\nduplication it targeted was the doctor's own copy of the worktree `git merge` policy; Gerrit\nchange 1665 (ticket `envious-metal-budgie`) replaced that fold with a worktree-free\n`merge-tree`/`commit-tree` merge into the published ref, so the duplicated merge no longer\nexists to extract.\n\nBeyond that, the two healers were found to share only about four lines of graph arithmetic while\nholding OPPOSED policies, so the original AC (\"no duplicated merge/unrelated-history logic\")\ncannot be satisfied behaviour-preservingly:\n\n- Unrelated histories: sync REFUSES on a non-empty local store (anti-graft rule); the doctor\n  UNIONS unconditionally, pinned by a held-out test. Same input, opposite required outcomes.\n- Merge mechanism: sync's consumers read ticket events off the tracker's WORKTREE files, so a\n  ref-only merge would leave readers on pre-merge state. Sync cannot adopt the doctor's engine.\n- Failure policy: sync must never raise (its read path swallows everything); the doctor must\n  raise so the push path abandons.\n- Plus an epoch-guard asymmetry, and different lock scope and head cardinality.\n\nFull evidence, with file:line citations, is in this ticket's comment\n\"Premise validation: a BEHAVIOUR-PRESERVING `reconcile_one` is not available\".\n\nTwo alternatives were considered and rejected by operator decision: a thin ~4-line\n`merge_class` extraction (buys nothing — it couples two opposed policy domains for four lines),\nand a deep unification (genuinely possible but behaviour-changing, a rewrite of the store's\nhottest path). Deep unification is NOT filed as follow-up work; it can be raised later if the\nduplication ever becomes costly.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] The premise is validated against current `main` and the outcome recorded on this ticket\n      with file:line evidence rather than in scratch notes.\n- [x] The disposition is explicit: obsolete, because the duplication this ticket targeted was\n      removed by Gerrit 1665.\n- [x] The rejected alternatives (thin extraction, deep unification) are recorded with the reason\n      each was rejected, so the question is not re-opened from scratch.\n- [x] No code change is made under this ticket."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786568462963007001,"uuid":"34cc5dfd-9654-46a5-8e81-a171f80513c1"}